WEBVTT

00:25:29.978 --> 00:25:31.589
The longer they stay in a field,

00:25:31.613 --> 00:25:34.283
the more likely they are
to take for granted assumptions

00:25:34.307 --> 00:25:35.657
that need to be questioned.

00:25:36.042 --> 00:25:39.603
Marathoners, on the other hand,
are experimental innovators.

00:25:39.627 --> 00:25:42.806
They usually discover their ideas
through trial and error.

00:25:42.830 --> 00:25:44.045
They often peak later

00:25:44.069 --> 00:25:46.697
because it takes time to test out
different approaches,

00:25:46.721 --> 00:25:50.463
like Darwin, spending decades
tracing the origins of species,

00:25:50.487 --> 00:25:53.062
or da Vinci experimenting
for years with different ways

00:25:53.086 --> 00:25:55.360
of modeling light in his paintings.

00:25:55.384 --> 00:25:58.275
But those habits allow them
to sustain their peaks longer

00:25:58.299 --> 00:26:01.490
and peak again later
as they explore new areas.